jadx-rs
Copyright 2026 the jadx-rs contributors

This project is a Rust reimplementation of the decompiler engine of jadx
(https://github.com/skylot/jadx), Copyright 2015 Skylot and contributors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The algorithms, pass ordering and data-model structure follow the original
jadx design; the original Java sources are used as a behavioural reference
(oracle) and are not part of this repository.

crates/jadx-core/resources/core.jcst is the class hierarchy data of the Android and Java
framework classes shipped with jadx (Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2015 Skylot and contributors).

RDX, Copyright 2026 Ch0pin and RDX contributors, licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0. The following parts of this repository are adapted from RDX
sources (Rust, non-GUI engine code); each adapted file names its origin and the modifications in
its module documentation:

- crates/jadx-package: the split-package container reader (bundletool `toc.pb` reader, split
  identity validation, logical split-aware entry paths, bounded ZIP directory check, temporary
  APK handling) is adapted from RDX `src/package_container.rs`. Modifications: the selection
  policy of the reference jadx plugins as default, `.apkm` support, manifest decoding with
  `jadx-resources`, a dependency free JSON reader, no dependency on the RDX engine.
- crates/jadx-index: the posting store (fingerprint keyed fixed size records, sorted runs on disk
  merged into one file that lookups binary-search) is adapted from RDX `src/invoke_index.rs`; the
  package scope filter from `src/package_scope.rs`; the bounded call graph (depth, node and edge
  caps, component classification, dispatch targets) from `src/call_graph.rs`; the call site, field
  access and integer literal scans from `src/native_xrefs.rs`, `src/field_references.rs` and
  `src/integer_references.rs`; the name and literal search ideas from `src/identifier_search.rs`
  and `src/search.rs`. Modifications: the index works on the `jadx-core` root and on instructions
  decoded by `jadx-dex-input` instead of the RDX engine, uses a dependency free fingerprint, a
  memory budget with external merge, and verifies every hit against the decoded code.

No fonts, icons, themes or GUI code of RDX are part of this repository.
